      {
        "id": 85474,
        "name": "Foote",
        "username": "Foote",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-01-03T16:21:20.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Paul\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/paul/48/5862_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Paul:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<blockquote>\nAre you working again with the same folks who did the minis for GSF?&nbsp;\n</blockquote>\nActually, entirely different people! The Tactics minis are being sculpted in clay, whereas the GSF minis were rendered as a 3d mesh on a computer.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Why the change? (I understand if you do not feel the need to answer that haha. Business and whatnot). Sculpting in clay first I would guess would yeild much more detailed minis than sculpting on the computer, but thats admittedly based on ignorance of the proccess. Very keen on seeing some progress pics once some sculpts are close to being finalized!</p>",
        "post_number": 22,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:09:09.955Z",
